WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.542
Narrator: One more feature to test: Describe this page.

2
00:00:03.542 --> 00:00:07.400
Narrator: A screen reader reads a page one item at a time, in a line.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.866
Narrator: It doesn't say that the essays fill most of the page,

4
00:00:10.866 --> 00:00:13.547
Narrator: or that a narrow column sits beside them.

5
00:00:13.547 --> 00:00:16.424
Narrator: A sighted visitor takes that in at a glance.

6
00:00:16.826 --> 00:00:20.188
Narrator: For someone who's blind, a picture of the layout is a map.

7
00:00:20.188 --> 00:00:23.203
Narrator: It says what's on the page before reading all of it,

8
00:00:23.203 --> 00:00:28.015
Narrator: and where things are when a sighted colleague says it's in the column on the right.

9
00:00:28.015 --> 00:00:30.450
Narrator: This button describes the layout in words.

10
00:00:31.127 --> 00:00:37.126
VoiceOver: Describe this page dialog pop up button

11
00:00:39.097 --> 00:00:43.697
Narrator: It's the second thing on the page, right after the skip link. I'll press it.

12
00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.327
Narrator: The dialog opened on screen… but VoiceOver didn't say so.

13
00:01:00.327 --> 00:01:04.694
Narrator: Someone listening wouldn't know it's there. I'll move on, to find it.

14
00:01:05.307 --> 00:01:07.884
VoiceOver: The home page web dialog with 9 items

15
00:01:07.884 --> 00:01:12.034
Narrator: There it is: a dialog called The home page. I'll step into it.

16
00:01:12.664 --> 00:01:16.463
VoiceOver: In The home page web dialog with 9 items heading level 2 The home page

17
00:01:16.463 --> 00:01:18.521
VoiceOver: Close button

18
00:01:18.521 --> 00:01:23.714
VoiceOver: This is the front page of a magazine. The newest essays take most of the page, and a narrower column beside them lists everything else.

19
00:01:23.714 --> 00:01:26.250
VoiceOver: heading level 3 From top to bottom

20
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.265
VoiceOver: list 7 items

21
00:01:28.265 --> 00:01:29.979
VoiceOver: 1

22
00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:35.979
VoiceOver: At the top, the site header: my name, which goes home, then links to Writing, Work, Signal, Tools and Resume, then Set for you, where you choose the drawings, theme and motion. Beside it is a button that pauses everything that moves.

23
00:01:38.252 --> 00:01:39.752
VoiceOver: 2

24
00:01:39.696 --> 00:01:41.639
Narrator: This is what the button is for.

25
00:01:41.639 --> 00:01:45.086
Narrator: It starts with a picture: the front page of a magazine,

26
00:01:45.086 --> 00:01:49.912
Narrator: the newest essays taking most of the page, and a narrower column beside them.

27
00:01:49.912 --> 00:01:53.296
Narrator: Then it walks the layout from top to bottom, in order.

28
00:01:53.907 --> 00:01:56.669
VoiceOver: Describe this page dialog pop up button

29
00:01:56.669 --> 00:02:01.266
Narrator: Escape closes it, and puts me back on the button. What it says is useful.

30
00:02:01.266 --> 00:02:05.863
Narrator: The gap is the opening: when the dialog appears, VoiceOver should say so.

31
00:02:05.863 --> 00:02:11.027
Narrator: And nobody who relies on a description like this has told me yet whether it helps.

32
00:02:11.027 --> 00:02:13.169
Narrator: That's the next test, with people.
